  "_note": [
    "Pirelli nominates three of the C1-C5 slick range for each Grand Prix and labels",
    "them HARD / MEDIUM / SOFT for that weekend only. The labels are therefore",
    "RELATIVE: 'MEDIUM' at Monza 2024 is C4, 'MEDIUM' at Silverstone 2024 is C2.",
    "They are physically different rubber, and pooling them as one compound is a",
    "specification error -- it biases cross-circuit comparison and makes transfer to",
    "an unseen circuit impossible.",
    "",
    "Since 2023 Pirelli has nominated three CONSECUTIVE compounds, so one number per",
    "event is sufficient: `hardest` is the C-number worn as HARD, and MEDIUM and SOFT",
    "are hardest+1 and hardest+2. tests/unit/test_compounds.py enforces that",
    "invariant, so a future non-consecutive nomination fails loudly rather than",
    "silently mis-labelling a season.",
    "",
    "`confidence` is per row. 'primary' means a Pirelli press release was read",
    "directly; 'secondary' means it came from reporting of one. Any row the data",
    "later contradicts should be re-checked before the table is trusted."
  ],
